{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "92a2c86f-4040-4ed4-b8e6-ec31e94cf83f"/*AssimpRoundTripExample*/,
  "Description": "Imports a model once with [AssimpImport] and carries its data through every connected type: MeshBuffers and MeshGeometry go back out through [AssimpExport] (Export Mesh writes the Geometry or MeshData with UVs, Export Points writes a point cloud), the MeshData's vertices become a point cloud through [MeshVerticesToPoints], and the Geometry voxelizes through [VolumeFromMesh] into a VdbVolume that branches into [VolumeToField], [VolumeToMesh] and [VolumeToPoints] - covering the field, mesh and point conversions. The preview draws the imported scene with its PBR materials via [DrawScene].\n\nThe DamagedHelmet glb from the Examples assets carries UVs, so the exported OBJ keeps the texture coordinates. Set a FolderPath and press Export Mesh or Export Points on the [AssimpExport] node to write the files.\n\nAKA: assimp, export, roundtrip, round-trip, obj, ply, convert, geometry, points, mesh, volume, field, uv\n\nSee also: [AssimpImport], [AssimpExport], [AssimpImportExample], [VolumeFromMesh], [MeshVerticesToPoints]",
